@startuml Capture & Refund Operations with Smart-Contract Integration

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Capture & Refund Operations - Smart-Contract Integration\n(Hybrid Pattern with Contract Lifecycle Tracking)

actor "Admin/API" as Admin
participant "CaptureController" as CC #FFE082
participant "EventDispatcher" as ED #C5E1A5
participant "CaptureRequestHandler" as CRH #FFF3E0
participant "ContractRepository" as CR #F8BBD0
participant "OrderRepository" as OR #E1F5FE
participant "PaymentService" as PS #FFF9C4
participant "Provider API" as API #E0F2F1
participant "PaymentCaptureHandler" as PCH #FFF3E0
database "osc_payment_contract" as ContractDB #FFE0B2
database "osc_payment_transaction" as TxDB #B2EBF2
database "oxorder" as OrderDB #B2DFDB

== PART 1: CAPTURE OPERATION ==

Admin -> CC : POST /admin/order/capture\n{orderId: "order789", amount: 99.99}
activate CC

note right of CC
  **Capture Trigger:**

  Can be initiated by:
  • Admin (manual capture)
  • GraphQL API (programmatic)
  • MCP Agent (AI-driven)
  • Auto-capture rule (on shipment)
end note

CC -> CC : Validate:\n• User permissions\n• Order exists\n• Amount valid

CC -> ED : **Emit** CaptureRequestedEvent(\n  orderId, amount\n)
activate ED

ED -> CRH : handle(CaptureRequestedEvent)
activate CRH

== Phase 1: Load Contract & Order ==

CRH -> OR : find(orderId)
activate OR

OR -> OrderDB : SELECT * FROM oxorder\nWHERE OXID = 'order789'
activate OrderDB
OrderDB --> OR : Order data
deactivate OrderDB

OR --> CRH : Order
deactivate OR

CRH -> CR : findByOrderId(orderId)
activate CR

CR -> ContractDB : SELECT * FROM osc_payment_contract\nWHERE OXORDERID = 'order789'
activate ContractDB

note right of ContractDB
  **Contract Record:**
  {
    "OXID": "contract123",
    "OXSTATE": "COMMITTED", ← Must be COMMITTED
    "OXORDERID": "order789",
    "OXPROVIDERORDERID": "pi_stripe_123"
  }
end note

ContractDB --> CR : Contract data
deactivate ContractDB

CR --> CRH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

== Phase 2: Validate Contract State ==

CRH -> CRH : Verify contract state:\n• getState() == COMMITTED?\n• hasOrderId()?\n• getProviderOrderId() != null?

alt Contract Not in COMMITTED State
  note right of CRH
    **State Validation:**

    Contract must be COMMITTED
    to allow capture.

    States that BLOCK capture:
    • DRAFT - No payment yet
    • PENDING - Conditions not met
    • FULFILLED - Already captured
    • CANCELLED - Contract cancelled
  end note

  CRH -> CRH : Log error:\n"Cannot capture - contract not committed"

  CRH --> ED : Handler complete (error)
  deactivate CRH
  ED --> CC : Error: Contract not ready
  deactivate ED
  CC --> Admin : 400 Bad Request\n{"error": "Contract not committed"}
  deactivate CC

else Contract Is COMMITTED

  == Phase 3: Check Authorization Details ==

  CRH -> TxDB : SELECT * FROM osc_payment_transaction t\nLEFT JOIN osc_payment_authorization_details a\n  ON t.OXID = a.OXTRANSACTIONID\nWHERE t.OXORDERID = 'order789'\n  AND t.OXTYPE = 'authorization'\n  AND t.OXSTATUS = 'completed'
  activate TxDB

  note right of TxDB
    **Authorization Record:**
    {
      "OXAUTHORIZATIONID": "auth_456",
      "OXAUTHORIZEDAMOUNT": 99.99,
      "OXCAPTUREDAMOUNT": 0.00,
      "OXREMAININGAMOUNT": 99.99,
      "OXEXPIRESAT": "2025-10-27...",
      "OXISEXPIRED": false
    }
  end note

  TxDB --> CRH : Authorization details
  deactivate TxDB

  CRH -> CRH : Validate:\n• Amount <= remainingAmount\n• Authorization not expired\n• Authorization not fully captured

  alt Validation Failed
    CRH --> ED : Handler complete (error)
    deactivate CRH
    ED --> CC : Error: Validation failed
    deactivate ED
    CC --> Admin : 400 Bad Request
    deactivate CC

  else Validation Passed

    == Phase 4: Call Provider API ==

    CRH -> PS : capturePayment(\n  providerOrderId: "pi_stripe_123",\n  amount: 99.99\n)
    activate PS

    PS -> API : POST /captures\n{\n  "payment_intent": "pi_stripe_123",\n  "amount_to_capture": 9999\n}
    activate API

    note right of API
      **Provider Capture:**

      Different providers use
      different capture endpoints:

      • Stripe: PaymentIntent.capture()
      • PayPal: Order.capture()
      • Adyen: Payment.capture()
      • Unzer: Charge.charge()
    end note

    API -> API : Process capture:\n• Deduct funds\n• Update payment status

    API --> PS : CaptureResponse\n{\n  "id": "cap_789",\n  "status": "succeeded",\n  "amount": 9999\n}
    deactivate API

    PS --> CRH : CaptureResult
    deactivate PS

    == Phase 5: Record Capture Transaction ==

    CRH -> TxDB : INSERT INTO osc_payment_transaction\n(OXORDERID, OXPROVIDERORDERID,\n OXTRANSACTIONID, OXTYPE, OXSTATUS,\n OXAMOUNT, OXCURRENCY,\n OXPARENTTRANSACTIONID)\nVALUES ('order789', 'pi_stripe_123',\n 'cap_789', 'capture', 'completed',\n 99.99, 'EUR', 'auth_456')
    activate TxDB

    note right of TxDB
      **Capture Transaction:**

      Links to authorization
      via OXPARENTTRANSACTIONID

      Transaction chain:
      auth_456 (authorization)
        └→ cap_789 (capture)
    end note

    TxDB --> CRH : Transaction saved
    deactivate TxDB

    CRH -> TxDB : UPDATE osc_payment_authorization_details\nSET OXCAPTUREDAMOUNT = OXCAPTUREDAMOUNT + 99.99,\n    OXREMAININGAMOUNT = OXREMAININGAMOUNT - 99.99,\n    OXUPDATED = NOW()\nWHERE OXTRANSACTIONID = 'auth_456'
    activate TxDB
    TxDB --> CRH : Authorization updated
    deactivate TxDB

    == Phase 6: Emit Payment Captured Event ==

    CRH -> ED : **Emit** PaymentCapturedEvent(\n  contract, order, captureResult\n)
    activate ED

    note right of ED
      **Event Emitted:**

      Triggers contract fulfillment
      and order finalization
    end note

    ED -> PCH : handle(PaymentCapturedEvent)
    activate PCH

    == Phase 7: Fulfill Contract ==

    PCH -> CR : find(contractId)
    activate CR
    CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
    activate ContractDB
    ContractDB --> CR : Contract
    deactivate ContractDB
    CR --> PCH : PaymentContract
    deactivate CR

    PCH -> PCH : contract.fulfill()

    note right of PCH
      **Contract Fulfillment:**

      State transition:
      COMMITTED → FULFILLED

      Marks contract lifecycle complete
    end note

    PCH -> CR : save(contract)
    activate CR
    CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE osc_payment_contract\nSET OXSTATE = 'FULFILLED',\n    OXFULFILLEDAT = NOW()
    activate ContractDB

    note right of ContractDB
      **Contract Fulfilled:**
      {
        "OXSTATE": "FULFILLED", ✓
        "OXFULFILLEDAT": "2025-10-20..."
      }
    end note

    ContractDB --> CR : Updated
    deactivate ContractDB
    CR --> PCH : Saved
    deactivate CR

    == Phase 8: Finalize Order ==

    PCH -> OrderDB : UPDATE oxorder\nSET oxpaid = NOW(),\n    oxtransstatus = 'OK'
    activate OrderDB
    OrderDB --> PCH : Order updated
    deactivate OrderDB

    PCH -> ED : **Emit** ContractFulfilledEvent(\n  contract, order\n)
    activate ED

    note right of ED
      **Side Effects:**
      • Email confirmation
      • Invoice generation
      • Analytics tracking
      • Audit logging
    end note

    ED -> ED : Notify subscribers
    ED --> PCH : Done
    deactivate ED

    PCH --> ED : Handler complete
    deactivate PCH
    ED --> CRH : Event chain complete
    deactivate ED

    CRH --> CC : Capture successful
    deactivate CRH

    CC --> Admin : 200 OK\n{\n  "status": "captured",\n  "captureId": "cap_789",\n  "amount": 99.99\n}
    deactivate CC

  end
end

== PART 2: REFUND OPERATION ==

Admin -> CC : POST /admin/order/refund\n{orderId: "order789", amount: 50.00}
activate CC

CC -> CC : Validate:\n• Order paid\n• Amount <= captured amount

CC -> ED : **Emit** RefundRequestedEvent(\n  orderId, amount, reason\n)
activate ED

ED -> CRH : handle(RefundRequestedEvent)
activate CRH

== Phase 1: Load Contract & Validate ==

CRH -> CR : findByOrderId(orderId)
activate CR
CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
activate ContractDB
ContractDB --> CR : Contract
deactivate ContractDB
CR --> CRH : PaymentContract
deactivate CR

CRH -> CRH : Verify:\n• contract.getState() == FULFILLED\n• Order has captured payment

alt Contract Not Fulfilled
  CRH --> ED : Error: Cannot refund unfulfilled contract
  deactivate CRH
  ED --> CC : Error
  deactivate ED
  CC --> Admin : 400 Bad Request
  deactivate CC

else Contract Is Fulfilled

  == Phase 2: Check Refund Limits ==

  CRH -> TxDB : SELECT\n  SUM(CASE WHEN OXTYPE='capture' THEN OXAMOUNT ELSE 0 END) as total_captured,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN OXTYPE='refund' THEN OXAMOUNT ELSE 0 END) as total_refunded\nFROM osc_payment_transaction\nWHERE OXORDERID = 'order789'
  activate TxDB

  note right of TxDB
    **Refund Calculation:**

    Total captured: €99.99
    Already refunded: €0.00
    Remaining refundable: €99.99

    Requested: €50.00 ✓
  end note

  TxDB --> CRH : Refund limits
  deactivate TxDB

  CRH -> CRH : Validate:\n• requestedAmount <= refundable\n• refundable = captured - refunded

  == Phase 3: Call Provider API ==

  CRH -> PS : refundPayment(\n  providerOrderId,\n  amount: 50.00,\n  reason: "Customer request"\n)
  activate PS

  PS -> API : POST /refunds\n{\n  "payment_intent": "pi_stripe_123",\n  "amount": 5000,\n  "reason": "requested_by_customer"\n}
  activate API

  API --> PS : RefundResponse\n{\n  "id": "re_abc",\n  "status": "succeeded",\n  "amount": 5000\n}
  deactivate API

  PS --> CRH : RefundResult
  deactivate PS

  == Phase 4: Record Refund Transaction ==

  CRH -> TxDB : INSERT INTO osc_payment_transaction\n(OXORDERID, OXPROVIDERORDERID,\n OXTRANSACTIONID, OXTYPE, OXSTATUS,\n OXAMOUNT, OXCURRENCY,\n OXPARENTTRANSACTIONID)\nVALUES ('order789', 'pi_stripe_123',\n 're_abc', 'refund', 'completed',\n 50.00, 'EUR', 'cap_789')
  activate TxDB
  TxDB --> CRH : Transaction saved
  deactivate TxDB

  CRH -> TxDB : INSERT INTO osc_payment_refund_details\n(OXTRANSACTIONID, OXORIGINALAMOUNT,\n OXREFUNDAMOUNT, OXTOTALREFUNDED,\n OXREMAININGREFUNDABLE, OXREASON)\nVALUES ('re_abc', 99.99, 50.00,\n 50.00, 49.99, 'Customer request')
  activate TxDB
  TxDB --> CRH : Refund details saved
  deactivate TxDB

  == Phase 5: Update Order & Contract ==

  CRH -> OrderDB : UPDATE oxorder\nSET oxtransstatus = 'PARTIAL_REFUND'\nWHERE OXID = 'order789'
  activate OrderDB
  OrderDB --> CRH : Updated
  deactivate OrderDB

  note right of CRH
    **Contract State After Refund:**

    Contract remains FULFILLED
    (refund doesn't change fulfillment)

    But we can track refund in contract
    for audit purposes
  end note

  CRH -> CR : find(contractId)
  activate CR
  CR -> ContractDB : SELECT contract
  activate ContractDB
  ContractDB --> CR : Contract
  deactivate ContractDB
  CR --> CRH : Contract
  deactivate CR

  CRH -> CR : addRefundToContract(contract, refundData)
  activate CR
  CR -> ContractDB : UPDATE osc_payment_contract\nSET OXMETADATA = JSON_SET(OXMETADATA,\n  '$.refunds', JSON_ARRAY_APPEND(\n    JSON_EXTRACT(OXMETADATA, '$.refunds'),\n    '$', JSON_OBJECT(\n      'amount', 50.00,\n      'refundId', 're_abc',\n      'date', NOW()\n    )\n  )\n)
  activate ContractDB
  ContractDB --> CR : Updated
  deactivate ContractDB
  CR --> CRH : Done
  deactivate CR

  == Phase 6: Emit Refund Event ==

  CRH -> ED : **Emit** RefundCompletedEvent(\n  contract, order, refundResult\n)
  activate ED

  note right of ED
    **Side Effects:**
    • Email refund confirmation
    • Update accounting
    • Analytics tracking
  end note

  ED -> ED : Notify subscribers
  ED --> CRH : Done
  deactivate ED

  CRH --> CC : Refund successful
  deactivate CRH

  CC --> Admin : 200 OK\n{\n  "status": "refunded",\n  "refundId": "re_abc",\n  "amount": 50.00\n}
  deactivate CC

end

note over Admin, OrderDB
  **Smart-Contract Capture/Refund Benefits:**

  ✅ **State Validation**: Contract state enforces
     capture/refund eligibility

  ✅ **Transaction Chain**: Parent-child relationships
     track authorization → capture → refund

  ✅ **Audit Trail**: Complete history in contract +
     transaction tables

  ✅ **Idempotency**: Contract state prevents duplicate
     captures (COMMITTED → FULFILLED once only)

  ✅ **Flexible Refunds**: Track multiple refunds in
     contract metadata

  ✅ **Provider Agnostic**: Works with Stripe, PayPal,
     Adyen, Unzer, etc.
end note

note over Admin, OrderDB
  **Capture/Refund Flow Comparison:**

  **OLD PATTERN (No Contract):**
  1. Load order
  2. Call provider API
  3. Update order status
  4. Done

  **SMART-CONTRACT PATTERN:**
  1. Load order + contract
  2. Validate contract state
  3. Check transaction history
  4. Call provider API
  5. Record transaction (with parent link)
  6. Update contract state
  7. Update order status
  8. Emit events → side effects

  **Why More Steps Is Better:**
  • Explicit state validation
  • Complete audit trail
  • Transaction relationships
  • Event-driven side effects
  • Idempotency guaranteed
end note

@enduml
